# Selection Lists Standards (Pull-downs, Dropdowns, Pickers)

Use consistent, accessible selection components across the app.

## Standard dropdown (Smart Scheduler style)

When you need a dropdown selection list like the Smart Scheduler grid (teal popover with a scrollable list and **yellow** selected option), use a Radix `Popover` dropdown and these styling conventions.

### Visual requirements (match Smart Scheduler)

- **Popover surface**: teal/brand surface with blur
- **Border**: `border-[var(--brand-strong)]`
- **Rounded**: `rounded-xl` (or `rounded-2xl` for larger menus)
- **Selected row**: `bg-[var(--cta)] text-[var(--cta-foreground)]`
- **Hover row**: `hover:bg-[var(--brand-strong)]/50`
- **Scrollable list**: `max-h-[300px] overflow-y-auto`

### Reference implementation (copy/paste)

```tsx
import { useState } from "react"
import { ChevronDown } from "lucide-react"
import { Popover, PopoverContent, PopoverTrigger } from "@/components/ui/popover"

type Option = { id: string; code: string; name: string }

export function SmartSchedulerStyleDropdown({
  label,
  valueId,
  options,
  onChange,
}: {
  label: string
  valueId: string | null
  options: Option[]
  onChange: (nextId: string) => void
}) {
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false)
  const selected = options.find((o) => o.id === valueId) ?? null

  return (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
      <span className="text-sm font-medium">{label}</span>
      <Popover open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
        <PopoverTrigger asChild>
          <button
            type="button"
            className="btn-pill flex min-w-[280px] items-center justify-between gap-2 border border-white/10 bg-card/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm shadow-sm ring-1 ring-white/5 transition hover:bg-card hover:ring-white/10"
            aria-expanded={open}
          >
            <span className="truncate">
              {selected ? `${selected.code} - ${selected.name}` : "Select..."}
            </span>
            <ChevronDown className="h-4 w-4 text-muted-foreground" />
          </button>
        </PopoverTrigger>

        <PopoverContent
          align="start"
          sideOffset={4}
          className="w-[320px] rounded-xl border border-[var(--brand-strong)] bg-[rgb(var(--brand-rgb)/0.95)] p-1 shadow-xl backdrop-blur-md"
        >
          <div className="max-h-[300px] overflow-y-auto">
            {options.map((opt) => {
              const isSelected = opt.id === valueId
              return (
                <button
                  key={opt.id}
                  type="button"
                  onClick={() => {
                    onChange(opt.id)
                    setOpen(false)
                  }}
                  className={`flex w-full items-center rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm transition ${
                    isSelected
                      ? "bg-[var(--cta)] text-[var(--cta-foreground)]"
                      : "text-foreground hover:bg-[var(--brand-strong)]/50"
                  }`}
                >
                  {opt.code} - {opt.name}
                </button>
              )
            })}
          </div>
        </PopoverContent>
      </Popover>
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Choose the right control

- **Native `<select>`**
  - Use when the list is small (roughly <= 20–30 options) and no search is required.
  - Prefer for Settings-style single selection (e.g., branch selection).
- **Searchable dropdown / combobox**
  - Use when list is large or users must search by name/code/email.
- **Multi-select with chips**
  - Use when multiple items can be selected (e.g., To/CC/BCC recipients).

## Required behaviors

- **Deterministic sorting**: always sort options predictably (usually by display name).
- **Stable keys**: never use array index as React key.
- **Clear empty states**:
  - “No options available”
  - “No matches”
- **Close behaviors**:
  - close on outside click
  - close on Escape (for custom dropdowns)

## Accessibility (required)

- Every selection control must have a visible `<label>` or equivalent.
- For custom dropdowns/comboboxes:
  - trigger must expose `aria-expanded`
  - list should be keyboard navigable (Arrow keys), and Enter selects
  - focus should move to the search input when opening (if searchable)

## Styling standards (this repo)

- **Native select**:
  - Use `className="ymca-select w-full text-sm font-semibold"` unless there is a strong reason not to.
- **Custom dropdown**:
  - Use the app’s brand surface + border
  - Provide a visible focus ring: `focus:ring-1 focus:ring-[var(--brand)]/50`

## Large-list performance

- Use `useMemo` for filtered lists.
- If the list is very large, prefer server-side search or virtualization (`@tanstack/react-virtual`).

## Reference patterns (in this repo)

- Multi-select + chips + search: `components/email-pdf-modal/RecipientPicker.tsx`
- Button + list dropdown: `ColorDropdown` in `app/settings/page.tsx`
- Native select: branch selection in `app/settings/page.tsx`
- Accessible popover primitive wrapper: `components/ui/popover.tsx`

